---
title: "High-Throughput Time-Series Ingestion: InfluxDB Line Protocol in Lateralus"
author: dextermos
date: 2026-11-22
abstract: A deep dive into time-series wire serialization with stdlib/influx_line.ltl, covering measurement escaping, tag indexing, typed field formatting, and nanosecond timestamp resolution.
---

## Overview

Modern observability platforms and time-series databases rely on standardized, text-based wire protocols that can be streamed with minimal overhead. The InfluxDB Line Protocol is the standard for high-throughput metrics ingestion.

Lateralus provides a standard library implementation in `stdlib/influx_line.ltl`.

## Line Protocol Anatomy

Format:
`measurement[,tag=val,...] field=val[,field=val,...] [timestamp]`

- **Measurement**: Name of the metric or table.
- **Tags**: Indexed key-value pairs sorted alphabetically for optimal indexing.
- **Fields**: Typed metric values (integers with `i`, booleans, floats, quoted strings).
- **Timestamp**: Integer nanoseconds (optional).

## Escaping Rules

- **Measurement**: Escapes commas (`,`) and spaces (` `).
- **Tag Keys & Values**: Escapes commas (`,`), equals (`=`), and spaces (` `).
- **Field Keys**: Escapes commas (`,`), equals (`=`), and spaces (` `).
- **Field String Values**: Escapes quotes (`"`) and backslashes (`\`).

## API Reference

- `influx_line.line(measurement, tags, fields, timestamp_ns)`: Serializes a record into a string.
- `influx_line.parse_line(line)`: Decodes a record into `{measurement, tags, fields, timestamp}`.
- `influx_line.field_int(v)`: Adds `i` suffix (`10i`).
- `influx_line.field_string(v)`: Quotes and escapes strings (`"value"`).
- `influx_line.field_float(v)`: Returns float string representation.
- `influx_line.field_bool(v)`: Returns `true` or `false`.

